# Copy to frontend/.env.local — never commit .env.local
#
# Local dev (backend on localhost):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Railway production (set in Railway dashboard -> Frontend service -> Variables):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.myglobalhealth.online
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.myglobalhealth.online
#
# Shared secret with the backend so its rate limiter can key proxied API
# calls on the real visitor IP (x-gh-client-ip) instead of this service's
# single egress IP. Set the SAME value on both Railway services (backend
# var: PROXY_CLIENT_IP_SECRET). Unset -> limiter keys on egress IP and the
# whole site shares one bucket (429s under normal traffic).
# PROXY_CLIENT_IP_SECRET=<random 32+ chars>
# AUTH_COOKIE_NAME=gh_auth  # must match the backend
#
# Edge session verification. The edge middleware decodes the auth cookie
# locally to role-gate navigation. Give it ONLY the PUBLIC key — the private
# signing key lives on the backend service alone, so a frontend compromise can
# never mint tokens. Use the SAME public PEM that is set on the backend service.
# A single-line var with literal "\n" for newlines is fine (normalised on read).
# AUTH_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=
#
# Nonce-based CSP script-src for the authenticated portals (/account, /admin,
# /doctor, /corporate). OFF by default — public routes always use the baseline
# CSP. Verify one logged-in portal page hydrates with no CSP console errors in a
# production build, then enable:
# ENABLE_NONCE_CSP=true
#
# S-002 break-glass: require admins to document a reason before viewing
# patient PHI (/admin/patients/[email] gate + backend guard deny). Must be
# set to "true" on BOTH the frontend and backend services together —
# backend-only flips 403 admin PHI reads with no UI to enter the reason.
# ADMIN_PHI_REQUIRE_REASON=true
#
# ── Build-phase tuning (P-001) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Since public country pages are statically generated again, `next build`
# prerenders ~550 pages that all read the same backend. That backend's pg
# pool is max 10 with a 5s connect timeout (backend/src/db/prisma.ts), so
# the build throttles ITSELF to stay under it. None of these are needed at
# runtime; all four are read only when NEXT_PHASE=phase-production-build.
#
# HARD INVARIANT: NEXT_BUILD_CPUS x NEXT_BUILD_API_CONCURRENCY must stay
# BELOW the backend pool max (10). Defaults are 4 x 2 = 8. Raising either
# one alone silently reintroduces the 503 "data is unavailable" reads that
# bake empty doctor/plan lists into static files. next.config.ts asserts
# this at build start and fails loudly rather than shipping thin pages.
# NEXT_BUILD_CPUS=4              # prerender worker processes
# NEXT_BUILD_API_CONCURRENCY=2   # in-flight backend reads per worker
#
# Per-read timeout during a build only (runtime stays at 4s so a slow
# backend never blocks a visitor's SSR). Nobody waits on a prerender, so
# waiting is free; baking a fallback into a static file is not.
# PUBLIC_CONTENT_BUILD_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
#
# Escape hatch. A build FAILS by default when any public content read falls
# back, because since P-001 that writes an empty page to disk instead of
# being a transient blip. Set to 1 only to ship past a knowingly degraded
# backend — it downgrades the hard failure to a warning.
# ALLOW_DEGRADED_BUILD=1
